.TH CLEVOD 8 "2026-09-13" "clevo-cc-linux 0.1.2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
clevod \- privileged Clevo control-center daemon (fan and performance mode)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clevod
[\fB\-\-driver\fR]
[\fB\-\-mock\fR \fIFIxture\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPath\fR]
[\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR \fIMs\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-poll\fR]
[\fB\-\-session\-bus\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clevod
is the only long-lived process that talks to the Clevo DCHU fan controller. It
polls the embedded controller, caches the last reading with an explicit
freshness state
.RI ( fresh / stale / unknown ),
persists user choices in a versioned TOML file, and serves
.B org.clevo.CC
on the system D\-Bus. The CLI and the graphical UI are clients and never touch
hardware directly.
.PP
Reads are open to any local user. The write methods
.BR SetFanMode (),
.BR SetPerfMode ()
are authorized through PolicyKit (actions
.BR org.clevo.CC.set\-fan\-mode
and
.BR org.clevo.CC.set\-perf\-mode );
when no authority is available they fall back to root only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-driver
Use the
.B clevo-cc
kernel driver sysfs/hwmon backend (read and write). This is the enabled write
path. Without it the daemon uses the read-only
.B acpi_call
backend.
.TP
.BI \-\-mock " Fixture"
Replay a recorded fixture instead of touching hardware; never writes.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " Path"
Configuration file (default
.IR /etc/clevo\-cc/clevod.toml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval\-ms " Ms"
Poll interval in milliseconds (default 2000).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-poll
Do not start the background poll loop.
.TP
.B \-\-session\-bus
Bind to the per-user session bus instead of the system bus (testing).
.SH D\-BUS INTERFACE
Service
.BR org.clevo.CC ,
object
.BR /org/clevo/CC ,
interface
.BR org.clevo.CC .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/clevo-cc/clevod.toml
Versioned daemon configuration; saved modes are re-applied on startup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clevo-cc (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR busctl (1)
